//! The five interpreter backends' committed capability tables (plan
//! §5.1's conformance moat: six published scores, no parallel claims).
//!
//! GENERATED by `cargo xtask gen-tables` from each backend's own
//! `caps::walk_capabilities()` replay (the registry-driven probe
//! corpus through the backend's REAL `lower_program` lane) — DO NOT
//! EDIT. The committed bytes are pinned equal to a fresh replay by the
//! drift test beside each backend (`crates/aeolus-<backend>/tests/
//! caps_table.rs`), and `cargo xtask verify-tables` gates the same
//! equality from the CLI side; a walk-verdict edit that forgets the
//! regeneration fails `cargo test` first.
//!
//! The rows' semantics: one [`PropCapability`] per IR longhand in
//! `Prop::ALL`'s own (cascade) order — the tier the backend's walk
//! answers and, for a refused longhand, the report's own boundary
//! text. An expressible longhand carries the empty reason. The
//! framework-free tables are the `aeolus audit --target <backend>`
//! face's verdict source and the `docs/CONFORMANCE-<backend>.md`
//! pages' renderer ([`crate::conformance::TableCaps`]).

